==Turkish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tr|ota|صاری|tr=sarı||yellow}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*siarɨg||yellow, white}}.<ref>{{R:tut-pro:SDM|*siarɨg|url=http://starling.rinet.ru/cgi-bin/response.cgi?single=1&basename=%2fdata%2falt%2fturcet&text_number=++95&root=config}}</ref> Cognate to {{etyl|xgn-pro|-}} {{m|xgn-pro|*sira||yellow}} (cf. {{cog|mn|шар||yellow}}), Altaicists consider the Mongolic form to be a cognate to Turkic,<ref name=*si̯ā̀jri>{{R:tut-pro:SDM|*si̯ā̀jri}}</ref> however borrowing from Turkic has also been proposed.<ref>{{R:trk:Clauson|entry=sarığ|page=848}}</ref> Under the controversial Altaic theory {{etyl|ja|-}} {{m|ja|白い|tr=shiroi||white}} (< PJ {{m|jpx-pro|*sìruà-}}) and {{etyl|ko|-}} {{m|ko|흰||white}} (< PK {{m|qfa-kor-pro|*hắi-}}) is also compared.<ref name=*si̯ā̀jri />
{{rel-top|cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|otk|𐰽𐰺𐰃𐰍|tr=sarıɣ||yellow}}, {{cog|xqa||tr=sarıɣ||yellow}}, {{cog|oui||tr=sarıɣ||yellow}}, {{cog|az|sarı||yellow}}, {{cog|ba|һары||yellow}}, {{cog|cv|шурӑ||white}}, {{cog|kk|сары||yellow}}, {{cog|kjh|сарығ ||yellow}}, {{cog|ky|сары||yellow}}, {{cog|tt|сары||yellow}}, {{cog|tk|sary|sāry|gloss=yellow}}, {{cog|tyv|сарыг||yellow}}, {{cog|ug|سېرىق||yellow}}, {{cog|uz|sariq||yellow}}, {{cog|sah|араҕас||yellow}}, {{m|sah|арыы||butter}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

